# The release job promotes "## [Unreleased]" and commits the result, so any
# local commit that also edited Unreleased conflicts on the next pull. A union
# merge keeps both sides instead of stopping, and tests/changelog.test.ts
# fails the build if that ever lands an entry inside an already-released
# section, which is the one way a union merge can be wrong here.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# Keep line endings stable across Windows and the Linux runners.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
